 text+=['## Coverage',f'{len(d)} verified observed pairs; {len(sample)} enter regressions. See coverage_all_30.csv for nonretained prior leaders and never-absent players. Small absence comparisons remain illustrated but excluded from fitting.','## Interpretation limits','Total passing involvement identifies the busiest passing participant, not necessarily the best offensive player. It reflects minutes and games played; totals are not per-minute rates. Raw on/off mixes lineup partners and replacement quality. The retained-first-ten rule can exclude a player absent early even if they return later; this is a stated eligibility choice, not evidence that they were traded. Current contexts are unmatched for other injuries, opponents and timing. Higher entropy is passing variety, not efficiency. Findings are exploratory; do not choose between volume, EC and on/off player definitions solely by stronger p values.','## Team data','|Team|volume-selected player|Prior on/off gap|Played/missed|Entropy played|Synthetic deleted|Actually missed|Equal-pass actual ΔH|','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
